BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Let's Get Dicey! with Board Games
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T193000
UID:6a8c84a54cb69d003e2300ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy board games? Join us for a relaxed afternoon of g
 ames\, where you can meet and play with other local folks in the communit
 y. All games are provided - just bring yourself!\nThis is a drop-in progra
 m for adults of all ages. No registration is required.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c84a54cb69d003e2300ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Friday Crafts - Watercolour Painting Crafts!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T153000
UID:6a80b22eaafa6100295cd786@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Watercolour crafts are back! We'll have a basic watercolour pa
 inting craft\, wooden blocks to paint\, and colouring sheets printed on wa
 tercolour paper. Paint with members of your community and get lost in the 
 dreamy colours!\nOther activities\, such as colouring and board games\, ar
 e always available at our Friday Crafts sessions. Come have fun and meet s
 ome new people from your community!\nDrop in.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a80b22eaafa6100295cd786
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brentwood Film Club Presents: Three Identical Strangers (2018)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T200000
UID:6a8c82e329a7dd0d674632f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of\nThree Identical Strangers\n(2018)\
 n“The astonishing true story of three men who make the chance discovery 
 that they are identical triplets\, separated at birth and adopted to diffe
 rent parents. The trio's reunion in motion a chain of events that unearths
  an extraordinary and disturbing secret that goes far beyond their own liv
 es.”\n96 mins (1.5 hrs)\nPG - Thematic content\, mild language\nThis fi
 lm will be screened with English closed-captions (CC) enabled.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, 1st floor\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c82e329a7dd0d674632f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
