BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Financial Planning for Business: Entrepreneurship 
 for New Canadians
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T193000
UID:6a8db7cf36204e08fbb70d05@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us online with the\nCanadian Foundation for Financial Pla
 nning.\nThis workshop introduces the essentials of launching a business\,
  including Goods and Services Tax (GST)\, Harmonized Sales Tax (HST)\, E
 mployment Insurance (EI)\, raising capital\, and choosing the right busi
 ness structure.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to join. O
 nce registered\, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link.\nNeed help 
 with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privac
 y Statement\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8db7cf36204e08fbb70d05
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty Coffee: From Your First Brew to Barista for Newcomer Ent
 repreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T193000
UID:6a91d0c737716d0d1ad7166e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to take your love of coffee beyond a cup of cappuccino? T
 hinking about opening your own café or launching a coffee brand? Explore 
 real-world career paths in coffee - from café barista to roaster to coffe
 e entrepreneur. Find your entry point in this industry and learn about wha
 t works\, what doesn’t\, and what to avoid.\nPresented by Hong Dai\, own
 er of Another Land Coffee\, a specialty coffee shop located in North York\
 , with over 15 years of experience in the specialty coffee and hospitality
  industry.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91d0c737716d0d1ad7166e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Understanding Taxes and Benefits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T153000
UID:6a8db2dabe1482002989ea61@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by\nWest Neighbourhood House\n\, this session will i
 ntroduce the basics of Canadian personal income tax and discuss the import
 ance of annual tax filing. Participants will also learn about the various 
 benefits for which they may be eligible.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual Zoom
  event is free to attend. After registering\, you will receive a confirmat
 ion email containing the Zoom link.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and 
 participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8db2dabe1482002989ea61
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
