BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk: Women and Children in Toronto's Riverdale in the 1800
 s: How Did They Fare?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T190000
UID:6a7f5b844027d701ebc460e2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all local history lovers\, join Dr. Elizabeth Muir as
  she discusses her book "Riverdale: East of the Don" which looks at women
 's and children's activities - work and play in Toronto's Riverdale commun
 ity. She will explain how women and children in the other areas of Toronto
  fared equally in the pioneer days with their successes and struggles.\nNo
  registration required\, but arrive early before space is full!
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f5b844027d701ebc460e2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pressed Flower Wearables Workshop - Bangle Cuff
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T150000
UID:6a7ba67b5d8bc300315a137a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join professional crafts designer Gabriela Delworth\, as you d
 iscover the basics of flower pressing including techniques\, best flowers 
 for pressing\, when to pick them and how to store them. Create a one-of-a-
 kind wearable piece with a colourful pendant of natural flowers.\nWhether 
 you are a jewelry enthusiast or a nature lover\, this session offers a cre
 ative space to design a wearable piece of art that lasts forever.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7ba67b5d8bc300315a137a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
