DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T143000
UID:6a9478e5660e510bf4408127@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Being new to Canada often means a lack of connections. Learn w
 hy the #1 skill that will help you thrive as a newcomer to Canada is netwo
 rking. Without question\, networking will help you achieve your profession
 al and personal goals.\nDo you want to find out why “it’s not what you
  know and it’s not who you know”? Join us for this fast-paced\, highly
  interactive skill-building workshop. Networking will help you strive\, th
 rive\, not just survive!\nProfessional Business and Career Coach\, and for
 mer TPL Entrepreneur in Residence (2013)\, Jean Chow\, offers speaking wor
 kshops on the topic of small business and skill building with a focus to s
 upport Newcomer audiences.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9478e5660e510bf4408127
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
