BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Shipra Vyas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T235959
UID:6a861802be1482002988931f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of September\, the works of artist Shipra
  Vyas are on display at Albion branch.\nShipra Vyas is a Toronto-based art
 ist whose work explores memory\, place\, and the everyday moments that sha
 pe identity. Working primarily in pencil and pastel\, she builds layered\
 , textured drawings that carry a reflective atmospheric quality. Her prac
 tice is informed by family life\, travel\, her Indo Canadian roots\, and l
 iterary influences\, drawing on these to create intimate studies of connec
 tion\, transition\, and belonging. Her work can also be found on Instagra
 m at @littlesketchdiary.\n"This series of drawings is inspired by Caitlin 
 Vernon’s debut poetry collection Hold On Until I Can Love You. Beginning
  with the book cover & illustrations\, the project grew into a larger bod
 y of work exploring themes of early relationships\, identity\, and place. 
 Created with pencil and pastel\, the pieces draw on Glasgow and Toronto\,
  using soft textures and layered greens to evoke a hazy\, memory-like atmo
 sphere that reflects and extends the poetry\, while also inviting viewers
  into a shared space."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\n
 program. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibi
 t their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect t
 he diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exh
 ibit can be viewed during Albion branch's open hours. Please check the\nAl
 bion branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit:
  Shipra Vyas\,\nThoughts\, Pencil and Soft Pastel\, Medium.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a861802be1482002988931f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
