BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T183000
UID:6a8cc022d4b10d003008d288@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Flemingdon Park branch and its neighbourhood is home to a 
 variety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry team to explore 
 the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize di
 fferent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importan
 ce.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. Registra
 tion is required.\nPresented as part of TPL’s environmental program seri
 es\, Our Fragile Planet. The series is generously supported by Friends of 
 Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nThe tour will start and end at th
 e Flemingdon Park\nBranch side entrance\nand will be guided by the City of
  Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces alon
 g the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program
  (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). Thi
 s program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weat
 her\, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.
LOCATION:Flemingdon Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8cc022d4b10d003008d288
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
