BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Sarah Saif
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T235959
UID:6a98400c5e6fc10d0550e863@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of\nSeptember\,\nthe works of\nSarah Saif
 \nare on display at\nMorningside branch\nThis is Sarah\, a Pakistani self-
 taught mixed media artist based in Toronto\, who's been painting for the b
 etter part of her life. Her art is an extension of her life\, her feelings
 \, her experiences ever since childhood\; it's always been tied to her\, e
 ven when she didn't realize it. She has started a business in hopes of sho
 wing the world a glimpse through her eyes. She is a creative with hopes of
  her paintings being displayed around the world\, one of which is being so
 ld in Bahrain.\n"I am inspired by life itself\, from everything I see and 
 feel\, my experiences and everything in between. Art can change someone if
  they are willing\, and I aspire to do that - to touch people through my a
 rt and help them feel understood in this world where one can feel so lonel
 y."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit program\n. Toronto Public 
 Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at location
 s across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural inte
 rests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nFree. All are welcome.\nTitle o
 f Piece: Disorder & Balance Medium (e.g. oil\, acrylic\, photography\, etc
 .): Mixed Media (Acrylic\, Paint Markers\, Oil Pastels) Size/Dimensions: L
 arge
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a98400c5e6fc10d0550e863
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thursday Night Adventurer's Club (Dungeons and Dragons)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
UID:6a6133043edb05633e8fee15@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come one come all!\nParticipants will get to experience collab
 orative storytelling at its finest.\nIn this limited Campaign\, participan
 ts will be crafting the world\, their characters\, and potentially the dir
 ection of the story.\nThe campaign will begin with a session of worldbuild
 ing\, character creation\, and a democratic vote on themes and setting. Th
 is will be known as our session zero.\nFollowing sessions will see our cha
 racters progress through a 10 month campaign.(September - June) Relationsh
 ips will be built\, challenges conquered\, and enemies defeated!\n*Program
  is intended for a mature audience\, no prior experience required.\n**Regi
 stration begins Monday August 17 at 12:00pm\n***Space is limited. As a res
 ult we request customers only register for one campaign. (Either Thursday 
 nights or Saturday afternoons.)\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6133043edb05633e8fee15
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
