BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Short Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T193000
UID:69de5e272866a5b4884877f0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in joining a book club but are short on tim
 e?  Then join our Short Book Club\, where we read titles that are 250 page
 s or less. Meetings are held on the second Wednesday of each month.\nOur S
 eptember book is\nA Deadly Affair\nby Agatha Christie\nSummary: Love can 
 propel us to our greatest heights . . . and darkest depths. In this new co
 mpendium of Agatha Christie short stories\, witness the dark side of love-
 -crimes of passion\, games of the heart\, and deadly deceits. This pulse-p
 ounding compendium features beloved detectives Hercule Poirot and Miss Mar
 ple\, master of charades Parker Pyne\, the enigmatic Harley Quin\, and the
  adventurous Tommy and Tuppence\, all at the ready to solve tantalizing my
 steries.\nNew members are most welcome! Please inquire at the circulation 
 desk if you would like a copy of the book.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Korean Tea and Traditional Tea Ceremony (Darye)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T143000
UID:6a85e902be14820029887d6b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please note that this program is only available on a first co
 me\, first serve basis for the first 25 participants.\nCertified tea somme
 lier\, Soo Park\, guides audiences on a journey learning and experiencing
  Korean tea and culture along with Korean tea history and tradition. Exper
 ience the Korean tea ceremony Darye and taste samples of different types 
 of Korean teas during the program.\nFood notice: the presenter will brew 
 and serve three types of tea during the presentation and Darye demonstrati
 on:\nWoojeon (green tea)\, Balhyocha (black tea)\, and Hwangcha (yellow te
 a)\n. All of these are 100% single-ingredient\, non-blended teas.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e902be14820029887d6b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
