DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T193000
UID:6a888e39b204780029947c16@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Virginia Van Vliet as we learn about intricate Victorian 
 mourning customs. After the death of Prince Albert\, Queen Victoria became
  known as “The Widow of Windsor”\, setting the tone for elaborate mour
 ning customs throughout the Empire. Come to learn about hair jewelry\, mut
 es\, crepe veils\, zinc tombstones\, tear bottles\, postmortem photography
  and other elements of the Cult of Mourning.\nNo registration required\, b
 ut arrive early before space is full!
