BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:5 Pieces of the AI Puzzle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T151500
UID:6a7240ffc7e02e3d006dd30a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Keith McDonald\, Founder of Toronto's the literac
 yAI project.\nA multi-media\, interactive program demystifying artificial 
 intelligence through an illuminating five-piece puzzle framework. This ses
 sion guides participants toward a better understanding of AI's presence\, 
 clarifies confusion\, and helps attendees navigate living\, working\, and 
 playing alongside it. Crucially\, attendees gain the foundation and agency
  to demand the AI they want. Registration is required. Runs 60- 90 minutes
  with questions.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7240ffc7e02e3d006dd30a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ciné-club / French Film Club: Le successeur
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T200000
UID:6a833f174cb69d003e2160a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Rejoignez-nous pour une présentation de\nLe successeur\n(2024
 )\, réalisée par Xavier Legrand. Quand Ellias\, nouveau directeur arti
 stique d’une célèbre maison de haute couture française\, apprend que 
 son père vient de mourir d’une crise cardiaque\, il se rend au Québec 
 pour régler la succession et découvre qu’il a hérité de bien pire q
 ue du coeur fragile de son père.\nUne discussion conviviale en français 
 suivra le film\, si le temps le permet.\nAucune réservation requise.\nJoi
 n us for a French-language film screening of\nLe successeur\n(2024)\, dire
 cted by Xavier Legrand. When Ellias\, the newly-announced artistic directo
 r of a famous French fashion house\, learns of the unexpected death of th
 is father\, he returns to Quebec to settle the estate to discover he inher
 ited much worse than his father's weak heart.\nAn informal discussion in F
 rench to follow the film\, time permitting. Film presented with English su
 btitles.\nDrop in.\nThis program is part of Culture Days\, a nation-wide f
 estival celebrating arts\, culture\, and creativity from September 18 to 
 October 4\, 2026. / Ce programme est présenté dans le cadre de la Fête
  de la culture\, une célébration nationale des arts\, de la culture et d
 e la créativité\, du 18 septembre au 4 octobre 2026.\nAccessibilité:\nL
 e sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue de
 s signes\, les services d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagneme
 nt sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moin
 s deux semaines à l’avance à : tpl.ca/accessibility-events
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a833f174cb69d003e2160a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Writing For Newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T143000
UID:6a516f350d65ac36003eded2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program provides a supportive\, low-pressure environment 
 where newcomers can build confidence in their English writing\, communicat
 ion\, and presentation skills. Together\, we will:\n1. Have a short\, coll
 ective discussion period.\n2. Begin writing based on a prompt from the ins
 tructor\n(Example: This year\, I learned... Last week\, I did... Something
  funny happened when…)\n3. Present what we wrote to the group.\nPlease n
 ote: This is a group meeting. We do not offer individual lessons. We will 
 not be spell-checking\, looking at punctuation\, grammar\, ect. We will be
  focusing on basic sentence structure and presentation.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (Youth Hub\, First Floo
 r)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a516f350d65ac36003eded2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
