BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T200000
UID:6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class\, you'll learn "vibe-coding": using an 
 AI coding assistant to build your own interactive story or simple game. Yo
 u'll design the branches\, describe the rules in plain language\, test for
  the tricky edge cases (what if the player picks the weird option?)\, and 
 end up with a single file you can share with anyone. Just a story you want
  to tell. This is the playful sibling of the practical vibe-coding worksho
 p.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and Risk Mess
 age\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activi
 ties that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do 
 not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are en
 couraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which i
 nclude best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy
  statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLe
 arn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn
  more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more 
 about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
