SUMMARY:Incorporation Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T160000
UID:6a986aa62dac6e00372391bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Opening up a business brings new opportunities\, but it also b
 rings challenges.  Incorporations Basics will cover the essential ins and 
 outs of starting a business. Learn the differences between a corporation a
 nd other types of businesses\, the important terminology for corporations\
 , how to properly register and set up a corporation\, and the basics of ru
 nning a corporation. The pros and cons of setting up a corporation will al
 so be discussed.\nThe presenter\, Samuel Michaels\, is the founding lawyer
  of SM Legal. Samuel practices primarily in corporate law and has a strong
  background in both corporate law and employment law. Samuel is also a pas
 sionate advocate for access to justice and legal education.\nDrop in. No r
 egistration required.\nThis program is part of Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First Floor Program Room (CPR)
