BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Run Your One-Person Business with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T180000
UID:6a9b51bb1c197d11325d7089@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When you're the whole company\, the admin never ends: emails\,
  scheduling\, proposals\, follow-ups. What if you could design a system to
  handle the busywork?\nIn this class\, you'll learn to design an administr
 ative system for a one-person business with AI as your assistant: intake p
 ipelines\, email drafting\, client communication\, and scheduling. Learn t
 o map work into four piles: what's rules-based\, what AI drafts\, what nee
 ds your judgment\, and what should never be automated. You'll build reusab
 le templates and leave with a clearer plan for how AI could help your busi
 ness.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers
  are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required a
 nd will start November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be 
 guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and Risk 
 Message\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes ac
 tivities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou
  do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants ar
 e encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, whi
 ch include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the pri
 vacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code
 \nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn m
 ore about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more
  about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about
  the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
