DESCRIPTION:Job hunting is a job in itself: applications\, deadlines\, int
 erviews\, follow-ups. What if you could build your own AI-powered system t
 o help you manage it?\nIn this hands-on class\, you'll explore a job-hunti
 ng dashboard built with AI: how it tracks applications\, sets automatic al
 erts for postings that match you\, and practices interviews with you throu
 gh role-play. You'll leave with the templates to build your own. We'll als
 o talk about how employers screen applications\, and how it can make thing
 s unfair. Come explore a tool that works for you\, not the other way aroun
 d.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and Risk Mess
 age\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activi
 ties that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do 
