BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Elmbrook at the Movies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T160000
UID:6a8f335a58433600542b6d17@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us with your friends each month\, to enjoy a film.  Sept
 ember we'll be showing The Princess Bride.\nThe Princess Bride is a wildly
  fun mix of romance\, adventure\, comedy\, pirates\, sword fights\, and ju
 st the right amount of inconceivable absurdity.  It follows Buttercup\, a
  young woman who believes she has lost her true love\, Westley - only for 
 a mysterious masked man to enter the picture and turn everything upside do
 wn.\nThe cast is packed with familiar faces\, including Cary Elwes as West
 ley\, Robin Wright as Buttercup\, Mandy Patinkin as Inigo Montoya\, Andre 
 the Giant as Fezzik\, Wallace Shawn as the delightfully sneaky Vizzini\, a
 nd Christopher Guest as the villainous Count Rugen.\nDrop In
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f335a58433600542b6d17
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
