BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: A Workout for Meaningful Dialogue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T104500
UID:6a904c9f36204e08fbb78f91@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Developed in Denmark\, and now offered around the world\, this
  fun\, active 45-minute training focuses on building the essential
  skills of everyday democracy.\nLearn to build consciousness and self-awar
 eness around your own perspectives while engaging in dialogue with others.
  Through a series of short\, interactive exercises\, you'll explore where 
 your opinions fall on a variety of topics. Guided discussions with others 
 who think similarly and differently from you will help you deepen your und
 erstanding of diverse viewpoints and strengthen your ability to engage in 
 constructive dialogue across differences.\n***\nAbout this event\nDigital 
 Expo 2026 is a dynamic day of learning\, exploration and connection focuse
 d on shaping a responsible AI future for everyone.\nFeaturing inspiring sp
 eakers and interactive exhibits\, as well as hands-on workshops for adults
 \, kids and teens\, the event explores how emerging technologies are trans
 forming our lives\, communities and civic institutions.\nTogether\, we'll 
 examine the opportunities and challenges of AI to foster a more informed\,
  inclusive and empowered digital society that protects Canadians and safeg
 uards democracy.\nCheck out tpl.ca/digitalexpo for more information about 
 the Expo and the workshops.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***\nAccessibility\nLive or auto
 mated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, intervener servic
 es\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your 
 request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904c9f36204e08fbb78f91
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
