BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matcha Workshop & Mini Japanese Tea Ceremony
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T140000
UID:6a91c7ab4cb69d003e240f3f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn about the origins of Matcha and create your own drink un
 der the guidance of Reina Sakao. Participants will learn how to make trad
 itional Matcha\, compare colour/aroma/ taste of different grades of Matcha
 \, and learn the best types of Matcha to buy.\nReina Sakao is a fourth-gen
 eration tea house and Urasenke tea instructor who trained at the Urasenke 
 School in Japan where her family owns and operates a tea plantation in Shi
 zuoka.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91c7ab4cb69d003e240f3f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Younger Adults: Telling Terrific Tales in Twine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T160000
UID:6a95923036204e08fbb87b88@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to create your own video game story! Artist and educ
 ator Jordan Sparks teaches participants how to use the open-source Twine g
 ame engine to design stories for video games. Participants will develop th
 eir own choose-your-own-adventure game with text\, images\, and sound. Thi
 s program is for younger adults aged 18-24.
LOCATION:Annette Street\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95923036204e08fbb87b88
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:African-Inspired Canvas Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T143000
UID:6a95b73baafa6100296073b2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:During this mixed-media art workshop\, learn to create your ow
 n canvas artwork by combining acrylic painting with vibrant African wax fa
 brics\, and personalize your piece with African-inspired patterns\, and wa
 x fabric accents\, creating a one-of-a-kind decorative artwork.\nThis crea
 tive workshop introduces participants to African-inspired artistic express
 ion through a brief presentation on the symbolism and aesthetic influence 
 of wax fabric.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95b73baafa6100296073b2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Navigating the Canadian Job Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T200000
UID:6a722b93e9de653600206166@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a discussion about the Canadian job market with\nE
 ddie Lee\n.  In this talk\, you will learn how to identify hiring trends w
 ithin the job market\, pursue potential career paths\, and how to interpre
 t labour market data.  Eddie is the founder and C.E.O of the consulting fi
 rm\nOneHub\nand has over thirty years of experience helping both employees
  and employers navigate the Canadian job market.\nRegistration on the TPL 
 website is encouraged.\nDrop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.\nFor m
 ore information\, contact the North York Central Library\, Business\, Scie
 nce and Technology Department (4\nth\nFloor) at\n416-395-5613.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a722b93e9de653600206166
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
